   "user": "O_oNevermore",
   "message": "today i shared a tweet with my rationalist friend about anthropic's statements about people using claude to build weapons\n\nand i was like \"holy shit people are using claude to build weapons\"\n\nand his response was like \"bro obviously everyone is already doing that and knows that\"\n\nand he is saying this without knowledge of anyone actually doing that\n\nand the reason why i found the news alarming and new and he didn't is because logically speaking AI has been around for a while and is capable of being used for building weapons and what not and you can therefore deduce that there is a non-zero amount of people that would be doing this\n\nso to him its propositional and so the news is basically not news to him\n\nto me its news because it changed my intuition, i have the same logical map as he does, but something changed when the info became common knowledge, because now the narratives that i can tell are new, because the knowledge in the minds of the general audience changed\n\nnow my intuition has access to knowledge that was previously only available by logical inference",
   "timestamp": "2026-09-11T15:25:23.843000+00:00",
